; block-kinds-band.fk — move, pivot, anchor, hold, and what a rig is missing.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/block-kinds.fk
;
; The taxonomy is Urs's, 2026-07-23 00:42. The rigs are measured: tonight's shell pipeline
; against form-run on a failing fkwu run, and the bearing chain from observe/bearing-chain.fk.
;
; Verdict 255 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  tonight's pipeline carries two of the four kinds
;     2  and is therefore not whole
;     4  its first missing kind is the ANCHOR — no known-good exit status to compare against
;     8  and three kinds' worth is missing in total (anchor + pivot)
;    16  form-run carries all four
;    32  and reports itself whole
;    64  the bearing chain carries three
;   128  and what it lacks is a HOLD: nothing stores a fix, so two bearings can never be
;        crossed into a point — which is why that cell yields a ray
;
; The teaching: bit 4 and bit 128 are the same mechanism used twice. Naming which KIND is
; absent names the repair, and the repairs are not interchangeable — an anchor is a truth
; to compare against, a hold is a second look. Tonight's pipeline produced correct verdicts
; all evening and could not have reported if it had not, and those are different properties.

(do
    (block-kinds-check))
